# Team backlog (fraBering issues)

Before planning new work, check team-approved backlog in addition to `AGENTS.md`.

## Sources (in order)

1. **`docs/team-backlog.md`** — markdown export (regenerate after triage on prod).
2. **`GET /api/issues/agent-summary`** — same content live (export token or admin auth).
3. **`GET /api/issues/:id`** — full issue with comments and attachment URLs (logged-in user).

## Regenerate export

Issue data lives in the **fraBering database** (production Postgres in prod). Team files items in the app at **Issues** in the navbar.

From repo root:

```sh
API_BASE_URL=https://frat.beringair.com \
ISSUES_EXPORT_TOKEN='…' \
node scripts/export-team-backlog/index.js
```

Local API:

```sh
ISSUES_EXPORT_TOKEN='…' node scripts/export-team-backlog/index.js --local
```

Admin login instead of token:

```sh
ISSUES_EXPORT_EMAIL=… ISSUES_EXPORT_PASSWORD=… API_BASE_URL=… node scripts/export-team-backlog/index.js
```

Commit **`docs/team-backlog.md`** and **`docs/team-backlog/attachments/`** after export so Cursor sees the current queue and screenshots.

Each active **`in_progress`** (or **`open`** with comments) item includes **Progress (changed, not resolved)** — latest comment plus **Latest screenshot** when attachments exist.

Full workflow: **`docs/issues-workflow.md`**.

## Agent rules

- **Build queue:** developer-approved + `open` or `in_progress`.
- **Ready for review:** shipped; reporter verifies — do not implement.
- **Needs clarification:** radar only — wait for reporter comments.
- **Done / closed:** out of scope.
- Items without **Developer approved** are not in the build queue — triage in `/issues` first.
